    "done_when": "Done when the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/concurrent-edits-meet-at-the-merge/parallel-nodes-on-one-module.html records both windows' counts, with the commands that produced them logged in the measuring run's own directory, whose path the fragment cites. The ledger window after must hold at least five pairs of runs with concurrent claims on one shared-root file, and the retained copies after show held-on-claim verdicts on shared-root file paths at zero backed by at least five runs that were admitted with a file claim under a shared root while another live run held the same file, counted only within the hours the verdict copies cover, so the zero and its exposure come from the same hours (the verdict log names a path only on a refusal, so the ledger's write paths and dispatch and landing times are the instrument). A hold whose holder claims the enclosing directory is excluded from the zero, since §2 keeps directory claims exclusive, and is listed separately. With fewer than five, the zero is reported as unmeasured, never as a pass. Negative control: the before window shows such verdicts above zero. A window with fewer than five concurrent pairs is reported as unmeasured and re-taken later, never as a pass. Every concurrent pair is accounted for, and any pair left with conflict markers or an unlanded head with no repair round fails the measure.",
